--- implementation and fixed Go build ---
Go source exports Hello()=42, RuntimeProbe(allocBytes), and NetDialProbe(host,port).
RuntimeProbe creates a buffered channel, starts a goroutine, waits on a 1 ms timer, allocates and writes allocBytes bytes, sends len(buffer), and returns the received length.
NetDialProbe calls net.DialTimeout("tcp", net.JoinHostPort(host,port), 2 seconds), closes a successful connection, and does not perform a DNS lookup for the measured numeric 127.0.0.1 input.
C++ runGoProbe uses dlopen("libgoprobe.so", RTLD_NOW|RTLD_LOCAL), intentionally never calls dlclose, copies dlerror and errno immediately after dlopen and each individual dlsym, invokes the exports in order, and creates a temporary 127.0.0.1 listener for NetDialProbe.
