--- HAP member identity correction and final objects ---
The first packaging check found Hvigor had stripped [GO_SO] from SHA-256 236db2d637b18a9fcb08bf44150152c2975274eaf7934853295420b9d4c980d9 and 3136128 bytes to member SHA-256 6d3122a0cb074dca30eddf0d672675c0697c631359a0264425472d7865448837 and 2160240 bytes.
That intermediate build was rejected for the measured input/member identity criterion and was not installed.
The local Hvigor 6.24.3 schema defines buildOption.nativeLib.debugSymbol.exclude as glob patterns excluded from strip when strip=true.
entry/build-profile.json5 was changed to strip=true with exclude=[**/libgoprobe.so], leaving the existing strip behavior enabled for all other native libraries.
A new clean and both HAP builds produced the final objects below.
